### **Complexity Analysis Explained**

Let:

- m = Number of meetings
- n = Number of rooms

**1. Sorting meetings: O(m log m)**

- We sort all `m` meetings based on their start time.
- Sorting `m` elements takes O(m log m).

**2. Finding an available room: O(n)**

- For each meeting, we may iterate through all `n` rooms to find an available room.
- In the worst case, we check every room.

**3. Finding the earliest available room: O(n)**

\- If no room is available, we iterate through all `n` rooms to find the one that becomes available earliest.

**4. Processing all meetings: O(mn)**

- We process `m` meetings.
- For each meeting, we may perform up to O(n) room checks.
- Therefore, O(m × n).

### **Final Complexity**

**Time Complexity:**

O(m log m + mn)

**Space Complexity:**

O(n) auxiliary space, excluding sorting overhead.

- O(n) for storing room availability information.
- Sorting may require additional implementation-dependent space.

**Interview explanation:** Since every meeting can potentially require checking all rooms, processing all meetings takes O(mn). Sorting the meetings adds O(m log m).

class Solution {
public:
    int mostBooked(int n, vector<vector<int>>& meetings) {
        sort(meetings.begin(), meetings.end());

        vector<long long> roomEnd(n, 0);
        vector<int> cnt(n, 0);

        for (auto &meeting : meetings) {
            long long start = meeting[0];
            long long end = meeting[1];
            long long duration = end - start;

            int room = -1;

            // Find smallest available room
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if (roomEnd[i] <= start) {
                    room = i;
                    break;
                }
            }

            if (room != -1) {
                roomEnd[room] = end;
            }
            else {
                // Find room that becomes free earliest
                room = 0;

                for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
                    if (roomEnd[i] < roomEnd[room]) {
                        room = i;
                    }
                }

                roomEnd[room] += duration;
            }

            cnt[room]++;
        }

        int ans = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (cnt[i] > cnt[ans]) {
                ans = i;
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

//Sorting + Two Min Heaps (Optimal)
**Time Complexity:**

- Sorting meetings: O(m log m)
- Initializing available rooms: O(n log n)
- Processing m meetings using min heaps: O(m log n)
- Finding the most booked room: O(n)

**Overall TC:** O(m log m + n log n + m log n)

**Space Complexity:**

- Available min heap: O(n)
- Busy min heap: O(n)
- Booking count array: O(n)
- Sorting overhead: O(log m) (typical implementation)

**Overall SC:** O(n) auxiliary space, excluding sorting overhead.

class Solution {
public:
    int mostBooked(int n, vector<vector<int>>& meetings) {
        sort(meetings.begin(), meetings.end());

        priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> available;

        priority_queue<
            pair<long long, int>,
            vector<pair<long long, int>>,
            greater<pair<long long, int>>
        > busy;

        vector<int> cnt(n, 0);

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            available.push(i);
        }

        for (auto &meeting : meetings) {
            long long start = meeting[0];
            long long end = meeting[1];
            long long duration = end - start;

            // Release rooms that are free
            while (!busy.empty() && busy.top().first <= start) {
                available.push(busy.top().second);
                busy.pop();
            }

            int room;
            long long newEnd;

            if (!available.empty()) {
                room = available.top();
                available.pop();

                newEnd = end;
            }
            else {
                auto [freeTime, roomNo] = busy.top();
                busy.pop();

                room = roomNo;
                newEnd = freeTime + duration;
            }

            cnt[room]++;

            busy.push({newEnd, room});
        }

        int ans = 0;

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (cnt[i] > cnt[ans]) {
                ans = i;
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};


